'' A VARIADIC CHARACTER IS THE SLOT'S WIDTH. fb_CHR and fb_WstrChr read each code
'' with cva_arg( ap, unsigned int ), and an i386 variadic slot is the machine word:
'' widen the codes to int64 there and every slot after the first is the previous
'' argument's high half. Measured on win32 -- chr( 65, 66, 67 ) came back as 65 0 66,
'' so tkEdit read every CRLF file as LF and saved it that way.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win32 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/chr-vararg-width.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"fb_CHR"(i32 3, i32 65, i32 66, i32 67)
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"fb_WstrChr"(i32 2, i32 %

'' The win64 control: there the variadic slot IS eight bytes, fbc pushes int64,
'' and this is the shape the lowering had before i386 was noticed.
'' STEP: -target win64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/chr-vararg-width.tiko
'' STEP-OUT: @"fb_CHR"(i32 3, i64 65, i64 66, i64 67)
'' STEP-OUT: @"fb_WstrChr"(i32 2, i64 %